 "name": "Black Belt",
 "type": "feat",
 "img": "modules/jjk5e/icons/techniques/divergent-fist.svg",
 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Prerequisite: Must have Martial Prowess</em></p>\n<p>Through much training, you gain the following martial options:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Takedown:</strong> Immediately after you hit a creature with a melee attack on your turn, you can try to grapple or shove the target as a bonus action.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Judo Throw:</strong> When you hit a grappled creature with a melee attack, you can grab the target and flip them on their back. If the target is Huge or smaller, it must make a Strength saving throw. On a failed save, you knock them prone, and if they fail it by 5 or more they are stunned until the end of their next turn.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Flying Drop Kick:</strong> You can use an action to jump up and land a Flying Drop Kick. You target a creature within your jump distance with an unarmed attack (Calculator <a href=\"https://fexlabs.com/5ejump/\">here</a>). The target takes your unarmed damage, and is pushed back 30ft.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
   "chat": ""
  },
